5519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787303659237282001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2b13fe1f-4ebc-4772-9a03-ff56e123bae2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"938d-d6e9-2580-4faa"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`docs/local-dev-env.md` (the \"Validating the whole tree locally / whether detached runs are\ntrustworthy\" section) lists the guards that misfire when another process touches the shared\ncheckout mid-run. It names two:\n\n- `_no_repo_root_leaks` (`tests/conftest.py`)\n- `_no_repo_commits` (`tests/conftest.py`)\n\nIt does not name the third member of the family: the session-level working-tree backstop in\n`tests/conftest.py::pytest_sessionfinish`, which diffs `git status --porcelain` across the\nwhole session and misfires on exactly the same concurrent commit, rebase, branch switch, or\neditor save. Its message has now been corrected to name that cause (bug\n`inner-honourable-bluejay`), so the doc is the one remaining place a reader can look up this\nguard family and not find it.\n\nUnlike the two per-test guards, this one fires ONCE at session end rather than blaming an\narbitrary straddling test, so it deserves its own line noting the different shape: the run\ntail shows a session-level REPO ISOLATION FAILURE, not an innocent test reported as errored.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocumentation only. No code change; the guard and its message are already correct.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The bullet list in `docs/local-dev-env.md` names the `pytest_sessionfinish` working-tree\n      backstop alongside the two per-test guards.\n- [ ] The entry states that it reports at session end rather than blaming a straddling test.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"add the session backstop to the concurrent-writer misfire list"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1868-2015-cadd-4456","ticket_type":"task","title":"Document the session working-tree backstop in local-dev-env's misfire list","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c2f93dac-16e3-4e41-9351-9a06c28a53e3","2b13fe1f-4ebc-4772-9a03-ff56e123bae2","2b908953-7211-4d4c-85c9-e3d53fe96644"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787306092700595001,"uuid":"5d3911b1-1b27-4054-8393-ca7959b67eae"}